**Summary**
After a head state repair operation, `loadLastState()` logs an incorrect currentFinalBlock that references a block which has already been deleted during the rewind.

**Root Cause Analysis**

- [NewBlockchain](https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/blob/2e5cd21edf21175fbbb0e6a95d2a110b97508d20/core/blockchain.go#L428-L430) calls loadLastState() to initialize currentBlock and currentFinalBlock from disk.
- When the head state is missing, [setHeadBeyondRoot](https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/blob/2e5cd21edf21175fbbb0e6a95d2a110b97508d20/core/blockchain.go#L464-L469) is invoked to rewind the chain to the last persistent state. This operation deletes all blocks beyond the recovery point.
- At the end of setHeadBeyondRoot, [bc.loadLastState()](https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/blob/2e5cd21edf21175fbbb0e6a95d2a110b97508d20/core/blockchain.go#L1116) is called again to log the current state.
- However, [this log statement](https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/blob/2e5cd21edf21175fbbb0e6a95d2a110b97508d20/core/blockchain.go#L684-L686) prints the stale currentFinalBlock value that was set during the initial loadLastState() call, before the rewind occurred.

**Logs:**

